Building Large Language Model (LLM) applications is fast and accessible, with
initial prototypes often created in minutes. However, moving an LLM application
from a WORKING PROTOTYPE to a RELIABLE PRODUCTION SYSTEM requires SYSTEMATIC
EVALUATION.

This study guide provides structured notes on the complete workflow for
evaluating LLM applications, based on the tutorial presented by CampusX.
It covers:
   🔵 Why evaluation is necessary
   🔵 The distinction between MODEL and APPLICATION evaluations
   🟠 A 10-step evaluation lifecycle, illustrated through an enterprise
      email classification case study (🟡 Zomato)
   🟣 Evaluator selection strategies
   🟢 Post-deployment monitoring mechanisms


