 1. 🔵 FUNDAMENTALS OF LLM EVALUATION
================================================================================

┌─ ⭐ DEFINITION ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Evaluating LLM applications ("LLM Evals") is the process of quantitatively   │
│ and qualitatively assessing the PERFORMANCE, SAFETY, CORRECTNESS, and        │
│ RELIABILITY of an LLM-powered system BEFORE and AFTER deployment.            │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

--- ❓ Why LLM Evaluation Matters ---------------------------------------------

  🔴 Unpredictability
       Non-deterministic LLM outputs can fail unpredictably across varied
       user inputs.

  🔴 Risk Mitigation
       Direct deployment without evaluation risks routing errors, inaccurate
       responses, and degraded user experience.

  🟢 Repeatable Optimization
       Systematic evaluation establishes a benchmark to measure whether prompt
       edits or model upgrades yield genuine improvements.

--- 🗂️ Categorization of LLM Evals --------------------------------------------

LLM evaluations fall into TWO distinct domains:

                         ┌──────────────┐
                         │  LLM EVALS   │
                         └──────┬───────┘
                 ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
                 ▼                             ▼
        ┌─────────────────┐           ┌──────────────────────┐
        │ 🔷 MODEL EVALS  │           │ 🟩 APPLICATION EVALS │
        └─────────────────┘           └──────────────────────┘

  🔷 MODEL EVALS
     • Evaluates base or foundational models (e.g., GPT-4, Llama 3, Claude 3)
       on broad academic benchmarks (e.g., MMLU, GSM8K, HumanEval).
     • Conducted primarily by AI research organizations and foundation model
       creators to gauge general reasoning, knowledge, and coding abilities.

  🟩 APPLICATION EVALS
     • Evaluates end-to-end LLM applications built for specific business tasks
       (e.g., customer support bots, email classifiers, RAG pipelines).
     • Conducted by AI engineers and application developers.
     • Focuses on task-specific correctness, adherence to business constraints,
       latency, and reliability.


