 3. 🟠 THE 10-STEP LLM APPLICATION EVALUATION WORKFLOW
================================================================================

Evaluating an LLM application requires a STRUCTURED, REPEATABLE LOOP.

   🔵 FRAME        🟣 SETUP              🟡 ITERATE LOOP               🟢 SHIP
  ┌────────┐    ┌──────────┐    ┌───────────────────────────────┐    ┌────────┐
  │ 1 Task │──► │ 3 Golden │──► │ 5 Run ► 6 Evaluate ► 7 Analyze│──► │9 Deploy│
  │ 2 Crit.│    │ 4 Method │    │   ▲                       │   │    │10 Mon. │
  └────────┘    └──────────┘    │   └──── 8 Improve ◄───────┘   │    └────────┘
                                └───────────────────────────────┘

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 1: Define Task and Target
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   🎯 Target : Specify the system, component, or workflow under test
               (in this case, the email classification pipeline).
   📌 Task   : Define the precise task being executed
               (here, multi-class text classification).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 2: Define Success Criteria and Evaluation Metrics
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ✅ Success Criteria : Establish what constitutes successful system
                         performance (e.g., correctly classifying customer
                         queries to avoid misrouting).
   🟣 Metric           : Select a quantitative metric suited to the task type.
                         For multi-class classification, ACCURACY is the
                         primary metric (e.g., percentage of correctly
                         classified emails out of total queries).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 3: Build the Golden Dataset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   ┌─ ⭐ DEFINITION ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │ A GOLDEN DATASET is a high-quality benchmark dataset consisting of       │
   │ representative inputs paired with manually verified expected outputs    │
   │ (ground truth).                                                          │
   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   Structure:
     📥 Input column           : Message (Raw email text).
     📤 Expected output column : Type (Ground truth label: Billing,
                                 Technical, or General).

   Size: Typically 50 to 500 rows for initial evaluation.

   🟢 Curation Best Practices:
     • Source data from real past production interactions
       (e.g., historical Zomato customer chats and emails).
     • Have human experts manually verify and annotate the ground truth labels.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 4: Define Evaluation Method (Evaluator Selection)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Select WHO or WHAT evaluates the system's generated output against the
   ground truth. Three primary evaluation methods exist:

   🤖 AUTOMATED (CODE-BASED)
      • Uses deterministic code (e.g., Python scripts) to calculate metrics
        like exact match, accuracy, or F1 score.
      • Best suited for structured or categorical outputs.
      • ✅ Applied in this case study because comparing single-word
        categories requires simple exact-match logic.

   👤 HUMAN EVALUATION
      • Human annotators manually inspect and score outputs.
      • High accuracy for complex reasoning, but 🔴 slow, costly, and
        non-scalable for continuous iteration.

   ⚖️ LLM-AS-A-JUDGE
      • Uses an external LLM to evaluate the primary system's output against
        expected answers.
      • Necessary when outputs are long-form unstructured text where simple
        code comparisons cannot evaluate semantic correctness.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 5: Run the Model / System
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Feed the input messages from the Golden Dataset into the LLM application
   pipeline to generate predicted outputs for every record.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 6: Evaluate Results
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Pass the generated predictions and ground truth labels into the evaluation
   method to compute the evaluation metric.

   🟣 Example: The initial test run yields an ACCURACY OF 80%
               (80 correct classifications out of 100 emails).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 7: Analyze Results (Error Analysis)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Examine the misclassified records (the 20% failure cases) to perform
   root cause analysis:

   🔴 Prompt Ambiguity         : The system prompt may lack clear distinction
                                 boundaries between Billing and Technical
                                 queries.
   🔴 Model Capability Deficit : The underlying LLM (e.g., a small open-source
                                 or low-parameter model) may fail to capture
                                 complex language nuances.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 8: Improve the System and Iterate
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Apply targeted fixes based on the error analysis:
     🟢 Option A: Refine the system prompt by adding explicit category
                  definitions or few-shot examples.
     🟢 Option B: Switch to a higher-capacity LLM.

   Re-run the evaluation against the SAME Golden Dataset. Because the
   evaluation dataset is fixed, results are directly comparable across runs:

     Run 1 (Base Prompt + Base Model) : 80%  ████████████████░░░░
     Run 2 (Refined Prompt)           : 90%  ██████████████████░░  ▲ +10%
     Run 3 (Upgraded LLM)             : 95%  ███████████████████░  ▲ +5%

   The team continues this loop until performance reaches the target threshold.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 9: Deploy the System 🚀
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Once the system satisfies accuracy targets (e.g., 95%+ accuracy), deploy
   the LLM application to live production.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 🟠 STEP 10: Production Monitoring and Data Flywheel
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Post-deployment monitoring is required to capture edge cases and failures
   in live traffic:

   🔴 Failure Detection         : When a misroute occurs in production (e.g., a
                                  billing email routed to Technical Support),
                                  the receiving team flags the error.
   🟡 Golden Dataset Expansion  : The flagged production email and its correct
                                  ground truth label are extracted and added
                                  into the Golden Dataset.
   🟢 Continuous Re-Evaluation  : The enlarged Golden Dataset is used to
                                  re-evaluate the application, driving
                                  continuous system reliability.


