 4. 🧩 MULTI-EVAL ARCHITECTURES FOR COMPLEX APPLICATIONS
================================================================================

┌─ ⭐ KEY PRINCIPLE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ A single LLM application often requires MULTIPLE distinct LLM evaluations.  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

While simple applications (like single-prompt classifiers) use one main
evaluation, complex systems require separate evaluations across individual
components.

--- 🟡 Example: RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) System Evals --------------

In a RAG application, multiple evaluations run concurrently:

                           ┌──────────────────┐
                           │ RAG APPLICATION  │
                           └────────┬─────────┘
        ┌──────────────┬────────────┴───┬────────────────────┐
        ▼              ▼                ▼                    ▼
   🔍 Retriever   🧬 Embedding    🔁 End-to-End RAG   ⏱️ Performance/Latency

  🔍 Retriever Eval
       Measures the vector search module's ability to retrieve relevant
       context chunks (e.g., Recall@K, Precision@K).
  🧬 Embedding Model Eval
       Evaluates vector space quality and similarity ranking accuracy.
  🔁 End-to-End RAG Workflow Eval
       Evaluates generator faithfulness, answer relevance, and context
       utilization.
  ⏱️ System Performance / Latency Eval
       Measures end-to-end response times, token throughput, and system
       resource costs.


