┌─ 🟢 BEST PRACTICES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ✅ Build Golden Datasets from Real Data: Always populate golden datasets     │
│    using anonymized real customer interactions rather than synthetic toy     │
│    data.                                                                     │
│ ✅ Lock Benchmarks for Regression Testing: Keep the evaluation dataset       │
│    consistent across iterations so performance shifts reflect genuine        │
│    prompt or model changes.                                                  │
│ ✅ Implement Production Flywheels: Treat evaluation as an active production  │
│    loop where live errors systematically expand the golden benchmark.        │
│ ✅ Decompose Complex Systems: Run modular evaluations on sub-components      │
│    (e.g., retrieval vs. generation in RAG) rather than treating the          │
│    application as a black box.                                               │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─ 🔴 COMMON MISTAKES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ❌ Deploying Without Evaluation: Relying on informal spot-checks ("vibe      │
│    checks") on 2–3 sample prompts before going to production.                │
│ ❌ Over-reliance on Manual Review: Relying entirely on manual human          │
│    inspection for routine iterative testing, creating engineering            │
│    bottlenecks.                                                              │
│ ❌ Ignoring Production Failures: Failing to capture live misclassifications  │
│    to update test datasets.                                                  │
│ ❌ Conflating Model Quality with Application Quality: Assuming a top-tier    │
│    base model automatically guarantees an accurate, error-free application   │
│    without proper prompt engineering and workflow evaluation.                │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


